{"archetypes":[{"name":"token-pricing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff replaces report token pricing with a Python pipeline that must preserve token-cost.sh as the sole authoritative calculator.","prompt_body":"Investigate the report token pricing path across python/report_tokens_cost.py, python/report_tokens_render.py, python/report_tokens_models.py, and related tests. Verify mixed bucket/blended arguments, environment rate forwarding, fallback warnings, and whether headline/table costs always come from scripts/token-cost.sh when it succeeds. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"issue-publish","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Issue posting now depends on byte-limit trimming, redaction, gh.issue_create, and quiet-mode-visible failures.","prompt_body":"Examine python/report_tokens_issue.py, python/gh.py, python/redact.py, and config changes for GitHub issue publication behavior. Focus on final redacted UTF-8 byte counting, immutable high-priority sections, truncation notices, single-pass redaction, and failure propagation to callers. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cli-wrapper","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The live /report-tokens entrypoint moved from embedded bash/Python to a thin shell wrapper plus Python CLI.","prompt_body":"Review skills/report-tokens/scripts/run-analysis.sh together with python/report_tokens_cli.py and python/report_tokens_scan.py. Check flag and environment parity, quiet-mode stream restoration, repo-slug failure behavior, empty-log handling, and removal of --plot-from without leaving stale paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"plot-isolation","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Matplotlib is intentionally isolated outside python/ while report_tokens_plot.py drives it through a subprocess schema contract.","prompt_body":"Inspect python/report_tokens_plot.py and skills/report-tokens/scripts/plot-cost-over-time.py plus the schema markdown. Verify the stdlib-only invariant for python/, subprocess invocation through the runner seam, MPLCONFIGDIR handling, persistent output paths, series shape by skill, and graceful skip behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ship-parity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Large new ship/finalize Python surfaces appear alongside the report-tokens work and may affect future or gated runtime paths.","prompt_body":"Review the new and modified ship-pr Python surfaces such as python/ship.py, python/finalize.py, python/merge.py, python/run_context.py, and their parity tests. Focus on whether behavior matches the existing shell contracts, whether writes and terminal states are safely scoped, and whether any Phase 7 or live-runtime gating assumptions are accidentally changed. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-harness","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change adds pytest to harness dependencies and wires many new tests and Makefile targets into CI.","prompt_body":"Check .github/workflows, requirements-test-harnesses.txt, Makefile, and the new report-token harness tests for CI integration risks. Verify shard target registration, dependency scope, timeout implications, executable bits, and whether the quiet-mode shell harness can run reliably in CI and locally. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
